{"id": "700000000000000137", "author_id": "u_federalreserve", "handle": "federalreserve", "name": "Federal Reserve", "followers": 1900000, "verified": true, "description": "Official account of the Federal Reserve Board.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T03:00:00+00:00", "text": "The Committee remains strongly committed to returning inflation to its 2 percent objective. Policy is data dependent; no decision has been made about the September meeting. Rates unchanged at 4.25-4.50%.", "lang": null, "like": 2400, "retweet": 1100, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "official", "query_tag": "fed-rate:official", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000000274", "author_id": "u_federalreserve", "handle": "federalreserve", "name": "Federal Reserve", "followers": 1900000, "verified": true, "description": "Official account of the Federal Reserve Board.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T04:00:00+00:00", "text": "Chair's remarks: we will act as appropriate to sustain the expansion. We are prepared to hold rates steady for as long as the data warrant, and to move if the inflation picture deteriorates.", "lang": null, "like": 1800, "retweet": 900, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "official", "query_tag": "fed-rate:official", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000000411", "author_id": "u_nyfed", "handle": "nyfed", "name": "New York Fed", "followers": 420000, "verified": true, "description": "The Federal Reserve Bank of New York. Official account.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T01:00:00+00:00", "text": "Survey of Consumer Expectations: one-year-ahead inflation expectations rose to 3.4% from 3.1%. Median expectations remain above the pre-pandemic average.", "lang": null, "like": 620, "retweet": 310, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "official", "query_tag": "fed-rate:official", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000000548", "author_id": "u_stlouisfed", "handle": "stlouisfed", "name": "St. Louis Fed", "followers": 310000, "verified": true, "description": "Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis official account.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T06:00:00+00:00", "text": "President's speech: with core services inflation still sticky, I would not rule out further tightening this year. I am not yet convinced we are on a sustainable path to 2%.", "lang": null, "like": 980, "retweet": 540, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "official", "query_tag": "fed-rate:official", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000000685", "author_id": "u_sffed", "handle": "sffed", "name": "San Francisco Fed", "followers": 240000, "verified": true, "description": "Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco. Official.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-28T23:00:00+00:00", "text": "New research note: the labour market has normalised faster than headline payrolls suggest. On our measures, wage pressure is no longer a source of upside inflation risk.", "lang": null, "like": 410, "retweet": 190, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "official", "query_tag": "fed-rate:official", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000000822", "author_id": "u_reuters", "handle": "Reuters", "name": "Reuters", "followers": 26000000, "verified": true, "description": "Top news from Reuters. The global news organisation.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T07:00:00+00:00", "text": "Fed funds futures now imply roughly a 38% chance of a rate hike at the September meeting, up from 24% before this morning's CPI print, according to CME data.", "lang": null, "like": 3100, "retweet": 1900, "reply": 0, "quote": 420, "cohort_hint": "pro_media", "query_tag": "fed-rate:media", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000000959", "author_id": "u_business", "handle": "business", "name": "Bloomberg", "followers": 8400000, "verified": true, "description": "The first word in business news. Bloomberg.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T07:00:00+00:00", "text": "Traders boosted bets on another Fed hike after core CPI came in hotter than forecast. Swaps now price about 40% odds of a September increase.", "lang": null, "like": 2200, "retweet": 1400, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "pro_media", "query_tag": "fed-rate:media", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000001096", "author_id": "u_nicktimiraos", "handle": "NickTimiraos", "name": "Nick Timiraos", "followers": 480000, "verified": true, "description": "Chief economics correspondent, The Wall Street Journal. Covering the Fed.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T08:00:00+00:00", "text": "Officials are unlikely to have made up their minds. The internal debate is between holding through year-end and one more insurance hike; nobody senior is arguing for cuts.", "lang": null, "like": 5400, "retweet": 2100, "reply": 0, "quote": 610, "cohort_hint": "pro_media", "query_tag": "fed-rate:media", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000001233", "author_id": "u_economics", "handle": "economics", "name": "Bloomberg Economics", "followers": 610000, "verified": true, "description": "Bloomberg Economics. Data and analysis.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T05:00:00+00:00", "text": "Our nowcast puts core PCE at 2.9% annualised over the last three months. That is above the level consistent with a hold, but not high enough on its own to force a hike.", "lang": null, "like": 890, "retweet": 430, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "pro_media", "query_tag": "fed-rate:media", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000001370", "author_id": "u_caixin", "handle": "Caixin", "name": "Caixin Global", "followers": 260000, "verified": true, "description": "财新传媒旗下国际财经媒体，记者报道全球市场。", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T06:00:00+00:00", "text": "美联储9月议息前瞻：市场定价加息概率升至四成，但多数受访经济学家仍预计按兵不动。", "lang": "zh", "like": 740, "retweet": 380, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "pro_media", "query_tag": "fed-rate:media", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000001507", "author_id": "u_reuters", "handle": "Reuters", "name": "Reuters", "followers": 26000000, "verified": true, "description": "Top news from Reuters. The global news organisation.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T09:00:00+00:00", "text": "ANALYSIS: Economists polled by Reuters overwhelmingly expect the Fed to hold in September. 58 of 71 respondents see no change; 11 see a 25bp hike.", "lang": null, "like": 1600, "retweet": 980, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "pro_media", "query_tag": "fed-rate:media", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000001644", "author_id": "u_biancoresearch", "handle": "biancoresearch", "name": "Jim Bianco (demo)", "followers": 340000, "verified": true, "description": "Macro research. Rates, credit, and why the consensus is wrong.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T08:00:00+00:00", "text": "Core services ex-housing has now accelerated three months running. The market is badly underpricing this. They hike in September and the long end sells off.", "lang": null, "like": 4100, "retweet": 1300, "reply": 0, "quote": 290, "cohort_hint": "en_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:en_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000001781", "author_id": "u_macroalf_demo", "handle": "MacroAlf_demo", "name": "Macro Alf (demo)", "followers": 290000, "verified": true, "description": "Ex-rates trader. Writing about macro and liquidity.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T06:00:00+00:00", "text": "No hike. Full stop. Bank credit growth is negative in real terms, and the Fed has never tightened into a credit contraction of this size. They hold and they wait.", "lang": null, "like": 3600, "retweet": 1100, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "en_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:en_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000001918", "author_id": "u_ratestrader_demo", "handle": "RatesTrader_demo", "name": "Rates Desk (demo)", "followers": 88000, "verified": false, "description": "Front-end rates. Opinions my own, not my desk's.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T09:00:00+00:00", "text": "Positioning matters more than the CPI print here. Everyone is short front-end. One hot number does not get you a hike, it gets you a hawkish hold.", "lang": null, "like": 1400, "retweet": 380, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "en_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:en_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000002055", "author_id": "u_ninja_economics", "handle": "Ninja_Economics", "name": "Ninja Economics (demo)", "followers": 210000, "verified": true, "description": "Economics, charts, and occasional sarcasm.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T10:00:00+00:00", "text": "The inflation data has re-accelerated and the labour market never broke. I make it about 60% they hike, and I think the committee is more hawkish than the dots imply.", "lang": null, "like": 2700, "retweet": 760, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "en_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:en_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000002192", "author_id": "u_lizannsonders_demo", "handle": "LizAnnSonders_demo", "name": "Liz Ann (demo)", "followers": 420000, "verified": true, "description": "Chief investment strategist. Markets, macro, and mean reversion.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T07:00:00+00:00", "text": "Watch the breadth of the inflation data, not the headline. On a trimmed-mean basis the picture is still disinflationary. That argues for holding rates steady.", "lang": null, "like": 1900, "retweet": 520, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "en_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:en_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000002329", "author_id": "u_biancoresearch", "handle": "biancoresearch", "name": "Jim Bianco (demo)", "followers": 340000, "verified": true, "description": "Macro research. Rates, credit, and why the consensus is wrong.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T08:30:00+00:00", "text": "To be explicit about the number: I'd put September at 65%. The market's 38% is a gift if you think inflation is re-accelerating.", "lang": null, "like": 2200, "retweet": 640, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "en_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:en_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000002466", "author_id": "u_hedgefundguy_demo", "handle": "HedgeFundGuy_demo", "name": "Buyside (demo)", "followers": 61000, "verified": false, "description": "PM. Macro. Long volatility, short narratives.", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T05:00:00+00:00", "text": "They are not hiking six weeks before the data revisions land. Hold, hawkish statement, and everybody pretends they saw it coming.", "lang": null, "like": 890, "retweet": 210, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "en_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:en_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000002603", "author_id": "u_hongguan_laowang", "handle": "hongguan_laowang", "name": "宏观老王", "followers": 180000, "verified": true, "description": "宏观研究，利率与汇率。前卖方分析师。", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T08:00:00+00:00", "text": "核心通胀连续三个月反弹，就业也没塌，我倾向于认为9月会加息一次。市场现在只定价四成，明显低估了鲍威尔的鹰派程度。", "lang": "zh", "like": 3200, "retweet": 880, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "cn_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:cn_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000002740", "author_id": "u_zhaisheng_note", "handle": "zhaisheng_note", "name": "债生笔记", "followers": 96000, "verified": false, "description": "固定收益。写给自己看的笔记，不构成建议。", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T07:00:00+00:00", "text": "别被单月CPI带节奏。美国信贷增速已经是负的，这个位置加息等于自找麻烦。我的判断是按兵不动，但声明会写得很鹰。", "lang": "zh", "like": 2100, "retweet": 520, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "cn_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:cn_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000002877", "author_id": "u_meilian_watch", "handle": "meilian_watch", "name": "美联储观察", "followers": 240000, "verified": true, "description": "每天更新美联储动态与市场定价。", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T09:00:00+00:00", "text": "CME FedWatch 显示9月加息概率已升至38%。历史上这个位置继续往上走的次数不多，但这次通胀结构确实更黏。我给50%。", "lang": "zh", "like": 4100, "retweet": 1200, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "cn_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:cn_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000003014", "author_id": "u_huaerjie_jiaoyuan", "handle": "huaerjie_jiaoyuan", "name": "华尔街交易员", "followers": 130000, "verified": false, "description": "十年交易经验，主做美股和美债。", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T06:00:00+00:00", "text": "加息。核心服务通胀没下来，工资增速还在4%以上，这种组合下按兵不动才是异常。", "lang": "zh", "like": 1800, "retweet": 460, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "cn_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:cn_kol", "is_reply": false}
{"id": "700000000000003151", "author_id": "u_hongguan_laowang", "handle": "hongguan_laowang", "name": "宏观老王", "followers": 180000, "verified": true, "description": "宏观研究，利率与汇率。前卖方分析师。", "author_created_at": "2020-08-20T12:00:00+00:00", "created_at": "2026-08-29T08:48:00+00:00", "text": "补充一句：如果9月不加，12月大概率要加，区别只是时间。政策路径的终点没变。", "lang": "zh", "like": 1100, "retweet": 290, "reply": 0, "quote": 0, "cohort_hint": "cn_kol", "query_tag": "fed-rate:cn_kol", "is_reply": false}
